<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Politburo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Political Bureau</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Politburo (Political Bureau) is the executive committee of a communist party's Central Committee and the real centre of power in a communist state. First created by the Russian Bolsheviks in 1917 and made permanent in 1919, the model was copied by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> and other communist states, where a small inner standing committee often holds supreme authority.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/politburo.jpg" alt="Politburo" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Politburo of the Central Committee of the All-Union Communist Party (Bolsheviks) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Execute_346_Politburo_passes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
